From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:21:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: port the IR HAL to AIDL

android.hardware.ir@1.0 was removed from hardware/interfaces, and the make
module also still asked for libhidltransport, which went years ago.

The generic android.hardware.ir-service.lineage is not a substitute here:
it drives /dev/lirc0 with LIRC ioctls, whereas this blaster is a UART at
/dev/ttyMSM1 and the pulse framing lives in libcir_driver. So the device
implementation stays and moves to AIDL, keeping transmitIr(), the 115200
baud rate and the 25-125 kHz carrier range exactly as they were.

Converting to Soong means the namespace has to import the blob tree's
namespace, which is where libcir_driver is declared; under make the
dependency resolved globally. TARGET_USE_LGE_IR guarded the make module
and had no other reader, so it goes with it -- every device sharing this
tree set it to true.
